## 3. How to Filter by Store Type

### Option A — Filter in SQL directly (works today)

```sql
-- All Exhibition customers
SELECT * FROM orders 
WHERE source_type = 'HISTORICAL' 
  AND order_name = 'Historical import - Exhibition';

-- JobBox + Changan combined
SELECT * FROM orders
WHERE source_type = 'HISTORICAL'
  AND order_name IN ('Historical import - JobBox', 'Historical import - Changan');

-- All historical sources as a summary
SELECT 
  REPLACE(order_name, 'Historical import - ', '') AS store_type,
  COUNT(*) AS customers,
  province
FROM orders
WHERE source_type = 'HISTORICAL'
GROUP BY store_type, province
ORDER BY customers DESC;
```

### Option B — Add a `store_type` column (recommended for dashboard)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> For cleaner dashboard filtering, we should run a one-time migration to add a `store_type` column to [orders](file:///Users/clustox_1/Documents/MasterGroup-RecommendationSystem/recommendation-engine-service/src/data_loader.py#383-432) and populate it from `order_name`.

```sql
-- Migration (run once)
ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS store_type VARCHAR(100);

UPDATE orders
SET store_type = REPLACE(order_name, 'Historical import - ', '')
WHERE source_type = 'HISTORICAL';

-- For live OE/POS orders
UPDATE orders
SET store_type = source_type   -- 'OE' or 'POS'
WHERE source_type != 'HISTORICAL';
```

Once this column exists, the dashboard can filter on `store_type` natively.

